This article discusses [[symmetric group:S3]], the symmetric group of degree three. We denote its elements as acting on the set <math>\{ 1,2,3 \}</math>, written using [[cycle decomposition]]s, with composition by function composition where functions act on the left. The multiplication table is given below. The convention followed here is that the row element is multiplied on the left and the column element is multiplied on the right. Since functions are assumed to act on the left, this implies that the column element is the permutation that operates first:

