===Order computation===

The symmetric group of degree three has order 6. Below are listed various methods that can be used to compute the order, all of which should give the answer 6:

{| class="sortable" border="1"
! Family !! Parameter values !! Formula for order of a group in the family !! Proof or justification of formula !! Evaluation at parameter values !! Full interpretation of conjugacy class structure
|-
| [[symmetric group]] <math>S_n</math> of degree <math>n</math> || degree <math>n = 3</math> || <math>n!</math> || See [[symmetric group]], [[element structure of symmetric groups]] || <math>3! = 3 \cdot 2 \cdot 1 = 6</math> || [[#Interpretation as symmetric group]]
|-
| [[general linear group]] of [[general linear group of degree two|degree two]] <math>GL(2,q)</math> over a finite field of size <math>q</math> || <math>q = 2</math>, i.e., [[field:F2]] || <math>(q^2 - 1)(q^2 - q)</math> || [[order formulas for linear groups of degree two]]. See also [[element structure of general linear group of degree two over a finite field]] || <math>(2^2 - 1)(2^2 - 2) = (3)(2) = 6</math> || [[#Interpretation as general linear group of degree two]]
|-
| [[dihedral group]] <math>D_{2n}</math> of degree <math>n</math>, order <matH>2n</math> || <math>n = 3</math> || <math>2n</math> || By definition. See also [[element structure of dihedral groups]] || <math>2n = 2(3) = 6</math> || [[#Interpretation as dihedral group]]
|-
| [[general affine group]] of [[general affine group of degree one|degree one]] <math>GA(1,q)</math> over a finite field of size <math>q</math> || <math>q = 3</math>, i.e., [[field:F3]] || <math>q(q - 1)</math> || [[element structure of general affine group of degree one over a finite field]]. || <math>q(q - 1) = 3(3 - 1) = 3(2) = 6</math> || [[#Interpretation as general affine group of degree one]]
|-
| [[general semilinear group]] of [[general semilinear group of degree one|degree one]] <math>\Gamma L(1,q)</math> over a finite field of size <math>q = p^r</math>, <math>p</math> prime || <math>p = 2, r = 2, q = 4</math>, i.e., [[field:F4]] || <math>r(q - 1)</math> || [[order formulas for linear groups of degree one]], see also [[element structure of general semilinear group of degree one over a finite field]] || <math>2(4 - 1) = 2(3) = 6</math> || [[#Interpretation as general semilinear group of degree one]]
|}

====Computation of prime powers in order====

The prime factorization of the order is:

<math>6 = 2^1 \cdot 3^1</math>

{| class="sortable" border="1"
! Family !! Parameter values !! Formula for order of a group in the family !! Formula for the largest power of a generic prime <math>\ell</math> dividing the order !! Case <math>\ell = 2</math> (answer should be 1) !! Case <math>\ell = 3</math> (answer should be 1) !! Case <math>\ell \ge 5</math> (answer should be 0)
|-
| [[symmetric group]] <math>S_n</math> of degree <math>n</math> || degree <math>n = 3</math> || <math>n!</math> || <math>\sum_{k=1}^{\lfloor \log_\ell n\rfloor} \lfloor \frac{n}{\ell^k}\rfloor</math> || <math>\lfloor\frac{3}{2^1}\rfloor = 1</math> || <math>\lfloor \frac{3}{3^1} \rfloor= 1</math> || no summands, so sum is 0
|-
| [[projective general linear group]] of [[projective general linear group of degree two|degree two]] over a [[finite field]] of size <math>q</math> || size <math>q = 2</math>, i.e., [[field:F2]], so the group is <math>PGL(2,2)</math> || <math>q^3 - q</math><br>In factored form: <math>q(q - 1)(q + 1)</math> || If <math>\ell</math> is the underlying prime of <math>q</math>, then <math>\log_\ell q</math>. <br>If <math>\ell = 2</math> and <math>q \equiv 1 \pmod 4</math>, then 1 + the exponent for the largest power of 2 dividing <math> q -1</math>.<br>If <math>\ell = 2</math> and <math>q \equiv -1 \pmod 4</math>, then 1 + the exponent for the largest power of 2 dividing <math>q + 1</math>.<br>Otherwise, if <math>\ell</math> divides <math>q - 1</math> or <math>q + 1</math> (can't divide both) the exponent for the largest power dividing that. If it divides neither, then zero. || Here, <math>\ell = 2</math> is the underlying prime of <math>q = 2</math>, so <math>\log_\ell q = \log_2 2 = 1</math>. || This is the case <math>\ell = 3</math> divides <math>q + 1 = 2 + 1 = 3</math>, and the power is 1.|| Since 2 - 1 = 1 and 2 + 1 = 3 have no prime divisors other than 3, there are no primes involved other than 2 and 3.
|-
| [[dihedral group]] of degree <math>n</math>, order <math>2n</math> || degree <math>n = 3</math>, order <math>2n = 6</math> || <math>2n</math> || largest power of <math>\ell</math> dividing <math>2n</math>. || 1 || 1 || no higher prime divides 6.
|-
| [[general affine group]] of [[general affine group of degree one|degree one]] <math>GA(1,q)</math> over a [[finite field]] of size <math>q</math> || <math>q = 3</math>, i.e., [[field:F3]]. || <math>q(q - 1)</math> || if <math>\ell</math> is the underlying prime of <math>q</math>, <math>\log_\ell q </math>. Else, if <math>\ell</math> divides <math>q - 1</math>, the exponent for the largest power dividing that. Otherwise, 0. || <math>\ell = 2</math> divides <matH>q - 1 = 3 - 1 = 2</math>, the exponent is 1. || <math>\ell = 3</math> is the underlying prime of <math>q = 3</math>, so <math>\log_\ell q = \log_3 3 = 1</math>. || <math>\ell</math> is neither the underlying prime of <math>q</math> nor does it divide <math>q - 1</math>.
|}

==Other operations induced by group multiplication==

===Self-action by conjugation===

<section begin="conjugation action"/>

Below is the induced binary operation where the column element acts on the row element by conjugation ''on the left'', i.e., if the row element is <math>g</math> and the column element is <math>h</math>, the cell is filled with <math>hgh^{-1}</math>.

Note that the action by conjugation functions by relabeling, so conjugating an element <math>g</math> by an element <math>h</math> effectively replaces each element in each cycle of the cycle decomposition of <math>g</matH> by the image of that element under <math>h</math>.

