===Interpretation as dihedral group===

{{quotation|Compare with [[element structure of dihedral groups#Odd degree case]]}}

The symmetric group of degree three is isomorphic to the dihedral group <math>D_6</math> of degree three and order six (i.e., it is the dihedral group <math>D_{2n}</math> of order <math>2n</math> where <math>n = 3</math>). In the table below, we denote by <math>a</matH> the generator of the cyclic subgroup of order three (which we could take as the permutation <math>(1,2,3)</math>) and by <math>x</math> one of the reflections (which we could take as <math>(1,2)</math>).

